# Cursor Rules — Hackways

Before generating code, making edits, or modifying infrastructure in this repository, you MUST inspect and strictly follow the canonical engineering specification in:

AGENTS.md

Core Rules:
1. Maintain the 6 independent services: apps/public-web, apps/core-web, apps/organizer-web, apps/admin-web, services/core-backend, services/global-backend. Never merge them.
2. Adhere to Azure VM limits (2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM): never compile Next.js on the VM, obey GOMEMLIMIT, cap memory.
3. Media uploads MUST use Azure Blob Storage direct SAS tokens. Never store uploads on the local VM disk.
4. Transactional emails MUST use Azure Communication Services (ACS) Email via the PostgreSQL outbox pattern. Never add local SMTP daemons.
5. RSVP capacity MUST enforce pessimistic locking via PostgreSQL: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE with statement_timeout = '2000ms'.
6. Use compile-time verified sqlc queries only. No raw SQL strings or ORMs.
7. Inspect existing code before patching; execute and verify real tests (go test ./... -race, npm test) before declaring complete.
